1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,219
Today is November 09, 2026.

3
00:00:07,219 --> 00:00:15,184
Overnight, Wall Street braced for a decisive week of inflation data, heavy Treasury supply, and political shockwaves.

4
00:00:15,184 --> 00:00:22,550
The S and P five hundred, Nasdaq, and Dow remain under pressure as rising yields weigh on valuations.

5
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:28,922
Following strong payroll data, markets now price an eighty percent chance of a December Fed rate hike.

6
00:00:28,922 --> 00:00:35,295
Traders expect the Federal Reserve to raise rates by twenty-five basis points if inflation stays hot.

7
00:00:35,295 --> 00:00:39,951
October C P I is this week's primary macro catalyst.

8
00:00:39,951 --> 00:00:47,709
Because last year's government shutdown disrupted price collection, several year-over-year C P I categories will not be published.

9
00:00:47,709 --> 00:00:57,513
Instead, the market is laser-focused on month-over-month headline and core C P I. Consensus expects both monthly readings to rise zero point three percent.

10
00:00:57,513 --> 00:01:02,476
A zero point three percent print will virtually lock in a December rate hike.

11
00:01:02,476 --> 00:01:09,474
Friday's P P I report will then test whether upstream factory costs are feeding consumer inflation stickiness.

12
00:01:09,474 --> 00:01:15,638
Frequent speeches from Federal Reserve officials around these releases will amplify intraday volatility.

13
00:01:15,638 --> 00:01:20,625
Liquidity faces a second major test from three Treasury auctions this week.

14
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:27,329
The Treasury auctions three-year notes today, ten-year notes Tuesday, and thirty-year bonds on Thursday.

15
00:01:27,329 --> 00:01:33,481
Weak buyer demand would push Treasury yields higher and compress technology valuations further.

16
00:01:33,481 --> 00:01:39,694
Conversely, strong institutional bidding would pull yields lower and spark an equity relief rally.

17
00:01:39,694 --> 00:01:45,981
In Washington, Republican midterm losses and a divided Congress triggered an immediate White House shakeup.

18
00:01:45,981 --> 00:01:52,292
Pragmatic Chief of Staff Susie Wiles is out, replaced by hardline nationalist Stephen Miller.

19
00:01:52,292 --> 00:01:58,530
Appointing Miller signals the White House blames internal coordination rather than its confrontational agenda.

20
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:05,907
Meanwhile, inviting U F C president and Meta board member Dana White as Press Secretary raises governance concerns.

21
00:02:05,907 --> 00:02:12,243
Markets fear erratic policy communication around tariffs, chip exports, and fiscal spending.

22
00:02:12,243 --> 00:02:20,319
Historically, under Truman, Nixon, and Clinton, divided government pushed presidents toward aggressive foreign policy actions.

23
00:02:20,319 --> 00:02:24,792
Yet the administration faces an impossible trinity in the Middle East.

24
00:02:24,792 --> 00:02:33,652
Washington cannot easily halt Iranian nuclear enrichment, keep the Strait of Hormuz open, and maintain military deterrence simultaneously.

25
00:02:33,652 --> 00:02:40,675
Secretary of State Marco Rubio and Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth face removal if oil prices spike.

26
00:02:40,675 --> 00:02:47,709
Meanwhile, Vice President Vance is pivoting away from foreign wars toward domestic technology and compute capital.

27
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:54,670
Overseas, Israeli President Herzog tasked opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot with forming a new government.

28
00:02:54,670 --> 00:03:02,047
Netanyahu's potential exit and Eisenkot's focus on pausing foreign conflicts reduce immediate Iran war risks.

29
00:03:02,047 --> 00:03:09,412
Traders are also watching trilateral U S, Russia, and Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday and Wednesday.

30
00:03:09,412 --> 00:03:16,422
Macro liquidity pressures are now colliding with a fundamental reckoning across the technology and semiconductor sectors.

31
00:03:16,422 --> 00:03:24,486
Even inside the Democratic party, local progressive groups are fighting AI data centers over rising residential electricity costs.

32
00:03:24,486 --> 00:03:29,829
On Wall Street, investors no longer reward raw AI revenue growth alone.

33
00:03:29,829 --> 00:03:37,194
Capital flows now demand proof that massive AI capital expenditures generate real free cash flow and net profit.

34
00:03:37,194 --> 00:03:44,400
Adding to sector pressure, Congress summoned Nvidia chief Jensen Huang for a closed-door briefing on November eighteenth.

35
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:51,300
Lawmakers are investigating his ties to Singaporean businesswoman Alice Huang following leaked private photos.

36
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:58,346
While Nvidia denies improper conduct, the probe introduces three major fundamental risks for chipmakers.

37
00:03:58,346 --> 00:04:06,300
Washington could tighten Asian export controls, apply a political valuation discount, and trigger supply chain sell-offs.

38
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:13,314
In actionable equities, traders should take profits and trim unhedged positions in Nvidia on any bounce.

39
00:04:13,264 --> 00:04:19,489
Export control uncertainty ahead of the November eighteenth hearing caps Nvidia's near-term upside.

40
00:04:19,489 --> 00:04:26,977
Second, A M D and Broadcom offer tactical buy opportunities if regulatory scrutiny targets Nvidia alone.

41
00:04:26,977 --> 00:04:41,670
However, if Congress signals industry-wide Asian export bans, investors must sell semiconductor beta across S O X X. Third, CoreWeave's Tuesday after-hours earnings report is the critical litmus test for upstream AI compute demand.

42
00:04:41,670 --> 00:04:49,869
If rising debt costs and cash burn outweigh GPU revenue growth, sell leveraged AI infrastructure plays immediately.

43
00:04:49,869 --> 00:04:57,136
Fourth, Thursday after-hours earnings from Cisco and Applied Materials will dictate institutional hardware positioning.

44
00:04:57,136 --> 00:05:04,918
Strong AI networking orders at Cisco and robust HBM equipment guidance at Applied Materials would trigger a buy signal.

45
00:05:04,918 --> 00:05:11,241
Use confirmed earnings beats there to accumulate Q Q Q and S O X X on support.

46
00:05:11,241 --> 00:05:19,048
In defense and energy, Israel's political shift toward de-escalation triggers a sell signal on geopolitical war premiums.

47
00:05:19,048 --> 00:05:26,315
Take profits in Lockheed Martin, Raytheon, ExxonMobil, and Chevron as Middle East strike probabilities fade.

48
00:05:26,315 --> 00:05:32,026
Navigating this macro minefield requires real skin in the game and strict risk discipline.

49
00:05:32,026 --> 00:05:39,440
Avoid speculative hype and concentrate capital in four to five deeply researched compounders over full market cycles.

50
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:47,418
When deploying one-point-five to two-times portfolio leverage, always pair positions with protective options hedges on S P Y.

51
00:05:47,418 --> 00:05:51,425
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

52
00:05:51,425 --> 00:05:55,592
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
